id: E14846-draft-2501_91199785
trigger_tool: autotools|make|conan
phase: build|testing
error_signature: "make test.*testmxml|testmxml:.*LIBMXML_STATIC|missing static archive in a shared build"
severity: 2
category: autotools|test-coverage|linkage
match_keywords: shared build, upstream test target, static archive, test executable, enable-static, Conan
title: A shared-library recipe may still need a static archive to execute the upstream test target
root_cause: >
  Some upstream Makefile.in projects select the static archive for their test
  executable regardless of whether the delivered library is shared. Turning
  off static output to simplify a shared Conan package removes an input to the
  registered upstream test target and can silently turn a required N/N test
  into an unbuilt or unexecuted test.
affected_scope: Legacy Makefile.in projects whose test executable explicitly depends on a static archive even in shared builds
verification_cmd: "inspect the test target's archive prerequisite; build shared and static outputs; sign the test ELF on OHOS; run the complete upstream test target and an installed shared-library consumer"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: preserve-test-link-archive-and-verify-delivered-shared-library-separately
rec_description: >
  Keep static output enabled while building the registered upstream test
  executable, execute every test group, and independently link an installed
  consumer against the shared package. Do not count a consumer smoke test as
  a substitute for the upstream target.
rec_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: "disable static output in a shared recipe and report the upstream suite as passing"
forbid_1_reason: the upstream test executable can depend on the omitted static archive
similar_to: E543-draft-B4CF
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E14846-draft-2501_91199785.md
source_event: mxml/4.0.6 target run mxml-w3-20261003T170803Z; log sha256 cc98559b7609ed1cf89c6c274ed63498e3a7b2c970a27c102edabe3c3b083e8c
ci_increment: Shared/static test closure can fail before compilation on HMDFS when generated config.status uses mktemp0700. Reuse the existing strict Autoconf temporary-directory repair for both primary and fallback anchors, exclusive task-private TMPDIR mkdir underumask007; retain generated-file cleanup and the complete static-linked upstream target. No shared provider cache or platform permissions are changed.
last_updated: 2026-10-12
draft: true
contributor_id: 2501_91199785
